    "message": "Make all four AI scenes use Claude's replies end to end\n\nAn end-to-end check through the Web/Project API (30 agents x 1 day) found\nfour places where a successful Claude call still had no effect:\n\n- Region search: candidates came only from text citations, which a JSON-only\n  reply rarely has, so the list was always empty. Also take the hosted\n  web_search_tool_result entries (allowed domains, deduplicated, max 25).\n- Report: the Run was marked completed before finish_review, and the UI\n  fetches the report once on that transition, so it showed \"not_generated\".\n  Write the report (or its unavailability) before marking completion.\n- Results chat: proofs had to be JSON-quoted strings; Claude cites recorded\n  strings verbatim, and one bad proof discarded every claim. Accept an exact\n  verbatim string; rounded, retyped or paraphrased values stay rejected.\n- Repeated identical requests: the ledger refuses a second paid call for the\n  same request, but draft previews and Run analysis kept no tape, so a repeat\n  fell back to rules. Persist those tapes in the Project store\n  (StoredResponseTape); replies that fail the sensitive-data check are not\n  written.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
